{
  "id": "icmp6",
  "label": "ICMPv6",
  "rfc": ["4443", "4861"],
  "notes": "ICMPv6 over IPv6 (protocol 58). All fields of the 8-byte common header are modelled. The four bytes after the checksum are modelled at their fixed offsets as Identifier and Sequence Number; for other message types those bytes carry type-specific data (MTU, pointer, and so on) that is not modelled. NDP messages (Router Solicitation through Redirect) and MLD share this header, which makes this entry cover the IPv6 control-plane traffic a GNS3 lab generates. The Code field is kept as a number because its meaning depends on Type.",
